  "hotelDescription": "From our Premier Inn London Holborn hotel, you'll have the best of the capital right on your doorstep. Make the most of our location with a trip to Covent Garden, catch some world-class ballet at the Royal Opera House, or explore priceless artefacts in the British Museum. You'll find plenty of theatres and venues nearby, including the Aldwych Theatre, Novello Theatre and Peacock Theatre. After a busy day out in London, head back to the hotel for a meal in our Thyme restaurant before enjoying a great night's sleep. Why not upgrade your stay by booking one of our Premier Plus rooms? You'll get to enjoy a dedicated floor of the hotel, a coffee machine and mini-fridge, Ultimate Wi-Fi, a rainfall shower with luxury toiletries, plus many other extras to make your stay even better.",
  "hotelOpeningDate": "",
  "hotelSPFDescription": "",
  "hotelDirections": "Exit Holborn Tube Station towards High Holborn and British Museum. Cross the main road and turn right towards High Holborn Street. Turn left into Red Lion Street (second street) on your left. You will find the hotel on right hand side. No onsite parking is available. \n\nTo enter Holborn from the north take the A41 towards Central London then A501 leading to A4200 towards Holborn, Bloomsbury. (Central London Congestion charges apply Mon-Fri 7am-6pm). \n\nTo get to Holborn from the south take M23 then A23 towards Central London. Follow the route via Kingsway towards A4200 Holborn, Bloomsbury. (Central London Congestion charges apply Mon-Fri 7am-6pm). \n\nThe site does not have any on site Premier Inn car park, however the 2 closest car parks to the Premier Inn are as follows: RCP Parking - Bernard Street WC1N 1LE. 15 GBP for 24 hours and is locked between midnight and 6am. To then reach our hotel will require a 12 minute walk to Red Lion Street or a 4 minute taxi journey likely to cost no more than 7 GBP. Bloomsbury Square Car Park - located directly on Bloomsbury Square WC1A 2RJ. 35 GBP for 24 hours. Bloomsbury is an 8 minute walk to the hotel.",
